# Task

## Summary
The generic actionable item, composed from the catalog's field blocks rather than its own compounds: `status` is a `statusField` configuration (Not Started → In Progress → Blocked / Done, with re-open), `priority` is the Priority field, `dueDate` the Due Date field and `createdAt` the Created At field. `assignee` links a CRM User; `tags` link base Tags.

## Nesting
Subtasks are `linksToMany(Task)` on the parent: the set is bounded, the "3 of 5 done" roll-up belongs on the card, and one editor maintains the list. There is no parent back-pointer, because two stored sources of one fact drift. Any depth works because each task carries its own subtasks.

## Usage
```ts
import Task, { TaskStatusField } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/tasks/task';

export class ReviewTask extends Task {
  static displayName = 'Review Task';
  @field document = linksTo(() => Document);
}
```
Extend Task additively and keep its lifecycle; a task that needs a different lifecycle is a different card. `TaskStatusField` is exported for boards and filters that group by status (see Status Board).

## Examples
`Task/spring-campaign-launch` is a parent with four subtasks, one in each status; `Task/approve-ad-budget` is the blocked one on its own.

## Non-goals
No time tracking (a work-log card links the task, not the reverse). No recurrence. No ordering field: display order is the consumer's list concern. Completion is whatever the person doing it says it is; the block never second-guesses a Done.
